# Markdown is not formatted by Prettier here, and the reason is mechanical
# rather than a matter of taste.
#
# Every doc in this repository was rendered from a template whose placeholders
# change width when they are substituted — `sky-boss-implementer` is 29
# characters in skeletor's source and however long your prefix makes it here.
# Prettier pads a markdown table's columns to its widest cell, so a table that
# is canonical before substitution is ragged after it. Left un-ignored,
# `format:check` is red in a tree nobody has touched, on files nobody wrote.
#
# Prettier's job here is JS, JSON and config. Prose is yours.
#
# Formatting your OWN markdown is fine — it has no placeholders in it. Narrow
# this to the paths skeletor shipped (`docs/`, `.claude/`, `.github/`,
# `CLAUDE.md`) if you want that, and accept that those stay ragged.
*.md

# Generated artifacts. Their generator owns their bytes; a formatter that
# rewrites them makes every regeneration a diff and every commit a fight.
docs/implementation_index.json

# Same rule, second generator. `scripts/gen_vscode_queries.py` owns the region
# between the markers in this file; Prettier reformats JSON, so leaving it
# un-ignored makes `format:check` and `dev check docs` disagree about the
# same bytes — one of them red whichever way you resolve it.
.vscode/settings.json
